{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And much cattle</b> the sons of Reuben and the sons of Gad had. Here Reuben was placed first. \"And the sons of Gad and the sons of Reuben said\" — Gad was placed first. Rather, at first Reuben was placed first because he was the firstborn, and afterward Gad was placed first because they were warriors and their slain were conspicuous, as written: \"and he tore the arm, also the crown of the head.\" 8 times the sons of Gad and the sons of Reuben are mentioned in this pericope, and this is: \"a hasty inheritance at first, its end shall not be blessed\" — מבוהלת is written with a ḥet for the 8 times they were mentioned concerning their inheritance to take at first; \"its end shall not be blessed\" — for they were exiled 8 years before the rest of the tribes."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:33.751326709Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}